From: Oliphaunt Maintainers <dev@oliphaunt.dev>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oliphaunt-wasix: honor noninteractive psql invocations

Wasmer reports captured standard streams as character devices, so psql treats
script input as an interactive terminal and writes prompts into captured output.
The Oliphaunt tool facades are deliberately noninteractive and need ordinary
psql file-input semantics regardless of the virtual descriptor type.

Honor one private environment marker with the exact value `1`.  Ordinary WASIX
psql invocations retain PostgreSQL's normal isatty-based behavior.
---
 src/bin/psql/startup.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/bin/psql/startup.c b/src/bin/psql/startup.c
index b0c07fb..49f7b99 100644
--- a/src/bin/psql/startup.c
+++ b/src/bin/psql/startup.c
@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@ main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	int			successResult;
 	char	   *password = NULL;
 	bool		new_pass;
+	const char *oliphaunt_noninteractive;
 
 	pg_logging_init(argv[0]);
 	pg_logging_set_pre_callback(log_pre_callback);
@@ -184,7 +185,9 @@ main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	/* We must get COLUMNS here before readline() sets it */
 	pset.popt.topt.env_columns = getenv("COLUMNS") ? atoi(getenv("COLUMNS")) : 0;
 
-	pset.notty = (!isatty(fileno(stdin)) || !isatty(fileno(stdout)));
+	oliphaunt_noninteractive = getenv("OLIPHAUNT_PSQL_NONINTERACTIVE");
+	pset.notty = ((oliphaunt_noninteractive != NULL && strcmp(oliphaunt_noninteractive, "1") == 0) ||
+				  !isatty(fileno(stdin)) || !isatty(fileno(stdout)));
 
 	pset.getPassword = TRI_DEFAULT;
 
